Aim:
To write a simple applet that draws text and shapes, and an applet that works as a colour palette.
8(a) Simple Applet
Algorithm
1. Start.
2. Import java.applet.Applet and java.awt.*.
3. Write a class that extends Applet.
4. In init() set the background colour.
5. In paint() set a colour and draw a string, an oval and a rectangle.
6. Write an HTML file with an applet tag naming the class file.
7. Compile with javac and run with appletviewer.
8. Stop.
Program 8.1 — HelloApplet.java (15 lines)
// Ex 8(a): simple applet that draws text and shapes
import java.applet.Applet;

Page 34 of 62

SCSVMV University | Department of Computer Science and Engineering | Java Programming Laboratory

import java.awt.*;
public class HelloApplet extends Applet {
public void init() {
setBackground(Color.WHITE);
}
public void paint(Graphics g) {
g.setColor(Color.BLUE);
g.drawString("Welcome to SCSVMV", 30, 25);
g.setColor(Color.RED);
g.fillOval(30, 45, 60, 60);
g.setColor(Color.GREEN);
g.fillRect(110, 45, 80, 60);
}
}
